# Rally Points > Download, Upload and Clear Rally Points on a vehicle (PLAN.md 13.4, D11).
#
# getRallyPointsToolStripMenuItem_Click tests (capabilities & MISSION_RALLY) >= 0, which every uint
# passes, so it always takes mav_mission.download of the rally list - MISSION_REQUEST_LIST with
# mission_type 2 - whose items fill MAV.rallypoints and do not touch the markers (GCSViews/
# FlightPlanner.cs:915-928); plan.rally.vehicle is that list's length.
#
# saveRallyPointsToolStripMenuItem_Click has one branch, the legacy protocol: setParam RALLY_TOTAL
# to the markers' count, then setRallyPoint per marker - RALLY_POINT, read back with
# RALLY_FETCH_POINT - and "Failed to save rally point" when a read-back times out (:5936-5957;
# MAVLinkInterface.cs:6346-6476). The SITL this runs against is ArduCopter 4.8.0-dev, built without
# the legacy rally messages: it never answers RALLY_FETCH_POINT, so the C#'s Upload sets
# RALLY_TOTAL and then fails on the first point, and so does this. (A firmware with the legacy
# protocol takes the points; the link's side of that is requests::tests::a_rally_point_* and
# plan.rs's upload_goes_through_the_link_as_the_c_sharp_sends_it.)
#
# clearRallyPointsToolStripMenuItem_Click sets RALLY_TOTAL to 0 and clears the markers and
# MAV.rallypoints (:2096-2110).
#
# Two rally points are put on the vehicle first with the mission protocol, through the draw
# panel's rally write, so Download has a known list to read. The vehicle is left with RALLY_TOTAL
# 0, as Clear Rally Points leaves it.
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/plan-rally-sitl.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_PLAN_DIR $WORK

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 500

click tab-plan
settle 1

# The vehicle's list, arranged: two points written with the mission protocol.
click draw-rally
click map@0.40x0.40
click map@0.60x0.40
expect rally.points 2
click rally-write
settle 4
click draw-waypoints

# Download: the vehicle's two, and the markers as they were.
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-rallyPoints
click menu-getRallyPoints
settle 4
expect plan.rally.downloading false
expect plan.prompt none
expect plan.rally.vehicle 2
expect rally.points 2

# A third marker, then Upload: RALLY_TOTAL goes to 3, and the first point is never read back.
click map@0.50x0.60:right
click menu-rallyPoints
click menu-setRallyPoint
key Return
expect rally.points 3
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-rallyPoints
click menu-saveRallyPoints
expect plan.rally.upload busy
settle 6
expect plan.rally.upload ~ RALLY_TOTAL=3
expect plan.rally.upload ~ ,0=timeout
expect plan.prompt Error
expect plan.prompt.text Failed to save rally point
key Return
expect plan.prompt none

# Clear Rally Points: RALLY_TOTAL to 0, the markers and the vehicle's list gone.
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-rallyPoints
click menu-clearRallyPoints
settle 3
expect plan.params.busy false
expect plan.params ~ RALLY_TOTAL=0
expect rally.points 0
expect map.rally 0
expect plan.rally.vehicle 0

# And the vehicle agrees: Download reads nothing.
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-rallyPoints
click menu-getRallyPoints
settle 3
expect plan.rally.downloading false
expect plan.prompt none
expect plan.rally.vehicle 0
